### Tested versions

4.7-dev3

### System information

Godot v4.7.dev3 - macOS Sequoia (15.7.3) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (10 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory

### Issue description

When using mathematical constants like `PI` and `E` in a simple `texture-blit` shader (introduced in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701), it immediately fails to compile properly. This might also happen for other built-in constants/uniforms, but I haven't checked. 


